    "narrative": "Our offensive output today hinges on **Corbin Carroll**, who sits at an elite 87.14 projection, benefiting from an exploitable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano (5.02 xERA). The combination of a favorable park factor and a top-of-the-order boost makes him our primary anchor. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Gabriel Moreno** also present high-upside plays against Nick Martinez and Sugano, respectively; both capitalize on positive park factors and favorable SP xERAs, pushing their efficiency scores comfortably into the 70s. **Brice Turang** remains a must-start at 67.46, as his leadoff role against Walker Buehler provides the necessary volume to chase stolen bases, our most critical category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.30. While he offers some platoon value, the optimizer favored **Zach McKinstry**\u2019s volume despite his mediocre score, largely due to the need for positional depth and concerns regarding the baseline floor requirements. We are navigating significant volatility today as several lineups\u2014specifically **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Mickey Moniak**\u2014are currently \"Lineup Pending.\" Should these projections shift due to defensive alignments or rest, we may be forced to pivot. Finally, keep a close watch on **Cole Young** and **Austin Riley**; both are battling tough matchups against pitchers with sub-3.50 xERAs, keeping their scores in the marginal 40-range. We continue to monitor **James Wood** on the IL, hoping for a return to health to bolster our OF depth.",
